{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>When you encounter.</b> This pericope is joined because of [the context] 'on the way.'" "<b>You encounter.</b> Like נקרא נקראתי, and they are from the root of מקרה and קרוב מפגע." "The alef of <b>fledglings</b> is added, like the alef in ובאזרועך, and the reason is that it is cruelty in the heart to take the mother upon the young, and likewise an ox or a sheep."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {2 "Reading רוטשה as 'crouching/brooding'; the word is unusual and the construction of the sentence is compressed, but the reference is to taking the mother bird while she is upon her young."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:19.085365321Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}